Subject: Describe every color buffer for a memory report

A memory report could say how many bytes the renderer's own device held for color buffers, but
not which ones: whose window, which app made it, whether anything still had it open, or whether
it was a task's current frame. FrameBuffer::describeColorBuffers lists every live ColorBuffer
under the locks that guard the table, with its size, formats, the bytes of its Vulkan memory,
its reference count, whether it waits for its close delay, the guest processes that hold it
open, and the display it is the current frame of. A small history beside the table remembers
which guest process made each ColorBuffer and when, and when it was last made a display's
frame; entries of destroyed ColorBuffers are dropped when the table is described or when the
history grows past twice the table. Nothing else changes.

